### Todo CRUD — spring-boot-3-data-jpa (JPA + global exception handling)
# Same API surface as the MVC project, but now backed by JPA + a database,
# with a @ControllerAdvice that turns errors into clean JSON.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Create a todo
POST {{host}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn Spring Data JPA",
  "description": "JpaRepository gives CRUD for free"
}

### Get all todos
GET {{host}}/api/todos

### Get one by id
GET {{host}}/api/todos/1

### Trigger the global exception handler — ask for an id that doesn't exist
# Expected: a clean ErrorMessage JSON (not a stack trace) thanks to @ControllerAdvice.
GET {{host}}/api/todos/999999

### Mark completed (PATCH)
PATCH {{host}}/api/todos/1

### Update via PUT
PUT {{host}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Learn Spring Data JPA (updated)",
  "description": "Now persisted to the DB"
}

### Delete by id
DELETE {{host}}/api/todos/1
